/P 393 0 R
/E (       In conclusion, Thoothukudi has experienced a marked increase in built-up area and a corresponding decline in vegetation and open spaces over the past decade. This land transformation has directly intensified land surface temperature and strengthened urban heat island effects. If these trends continue, the region may face severe environmental and socio-economic challenges. Therefore, immediate implementation of sustainable urban planning and climate-resilient strategies is essential to ensure long-term ecological balance and urban sustainability.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [1]
>>
